issue.description:
Proposed by bob-cli-47.3 (PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP note #1) and triaged by the bob-cli-47 land agent.

Repo: bob-plugins (linked). Before the bob-cli-47 split, `BulletPropertyPickerModal` in
`plugins/bob-navigation-hotkeys/main.js` defined `onClose()` twice (main.js at c3349aa /
c1762af^, about lines 27575 and 30051). In a class body the later definition wins, so the
first one has been dead since c0ff974 ("render compact Task Card view", 2026-10-03). The
dead body was the Task Card cleanup:

```js
onClose() {
  if (this.modalEl) {
    this.modalEl.removeClass("bob-task-card-modal");
    this.modalEl.removeClass("bob-task-card-wide");
  }
  this.linkResolving = false;
  this.taskCardDispatching = false;
  if (this.plugin && this.plugin.activeBulletPropertyPicker === this) {
    this.plugin.activeBulletPropertyPicker = null;
  }
  super.onClose();
}
```

The split (c1762af) kept behavior byte-identical: it kept only the live body, which now
sits in `plugins/bob-navigation-hotkeys/src/350-picker-task-card.js` (`onClose`, about
line 608). That body clears `activeBulletPropertyPicker`, sets `vaultStageRefreshId = -1`,
calls `clearPendingBatch()`, then `super.onClose()`. It never removes the
`bob-task-card-modal` / `bob-task-card-wide` classes and never resets `linkResolving` or
`taskCardDispatching`.

Root cause: the Task Card cleanup was added as a second `onClose` method instead of being
merged into the existing one. Likely fix: fold the dead body's class removal and flag
resets into the live `onClose` in the 350 fragment, run `npm run build`, add a focused
test, and patch-bump the plugin.
